    <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Dumbbell Tricep Kickback</h1>
  <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u> 
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Seated Dumbbell Tricep Kickback. The video highlights the triceps muscles in bright glowing colors, illustrating how bending forward on a flat bench isolates the back of the arm as the dumbbells are extended backward until full arm extension.

Exercise Name: Seated Dumbbell Tricep Kickback
Target Muscles: Triceps Brachii (Long, Lateral, and Medial heads)
Secondary Muscles: Posterior Deltoids (Rear Shoulders), Rhomboids & Upper Back (for stabilization)

</div></div>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

<u><b><h4>Step 1: Setup</h4></b></u>
Sit at the edge of a flat bench with your feet planted firmly on the floor. Hinge forward at your hips while keeping your back flat and chest close to your knees. Hold a dumbbell in each hand.

<u><b><h4>Step 2: Elbow Positioning & Alignment</h4></b></u>
Raise your upper arms so they are parallel to your torso and keep your elbows pinned tightly to your sides throughout the entire set.

<u><b><h4>Step 3: Kickback Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>
Exhale as you extend your elbows, pushing the dumbbells backward in a controlled arc until your arms are fully straight. Squeeze your triceps tightly at peak extension.

<u><b><h4>Step 4: Return Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>
Inhale as you slowly lower the dumbbells back to a 90-degree angle at the elbow, keeping your upper arms stationary and avoiding momentum or swinging.


<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

<b>◉Peak Triceps Contraction:</b> Maximum mechanical tension occurs at full arm extension, offering an intense lockout squeeze.<br>

<b>◉Seated Core Support:</b> Sitting hinged forward reduces lower back strain and prevents body swinging/cheating compared to the standing variation.<br>

<b>◉Unilateral Balance:</b> Using dumbbells ensures both arms work equally, correcting strength imbalances between your right and left triceps.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 4 | 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your elbows stationary and high throughout the movement—only your forearms should move.


